CART_CHECKOUT_TEXT = [
    ("Cart Data Model",
     "Cart is NOT a parent entity with child items — each cart row IS one item. Schema: id, product_id, user_id "
     "(nullable for guests), session_id (for guests), title, category_id, category, license (1=Personal, "
     "2=Commercial), is_extended, extended_amount, price, seller_fee, buyer_fee, quantity, coupon_id, discount, "
     "reskin_selected, publish_selected, store_optimization_selected, timestamps. A single user can have multiple "
     "cart rows (one per product). Same product cannot be in cart twice — getDataForCart() checks for existing "
     "row by product_id + user_id/session_id and returns false if found."),
    ("Price Calculation",
     "Personal license: price = product.price. If active campaign: price = campaign_product_price[1] - "
     "personalBuyerFee (campaign price minus personal buyer fee). Commercial license: price = product.price_cl. "
     "If active campaign: price = campaign_product_commercial_price[1] - commercialBuyerFee. Buyer fee added "
     "separately: personalBuyerFee = category.personal_buyer_fee, commercialBuyerFee = category.commercial_buyer_fee. "
     "Extended license (12-month): extended_amount = category.twelve_month_extended_fee (only if is_extended=1). "
     "Addon services: reskin_price + publish_price + store_optimization_price from product fields (only if "
     "respective flag = 1)."),
    ("Coupon System",
     "Coupon applied via GET /cart/apply-coupon?coupon_code=X&subtotal=Y&cart_ids=[1,2,3]. Validates: coupon "
     "exists, status=1, start_date <= now <= end_date, subtotal >= minimum_spend, total usage count < "
     "usage_limit_per_coupon (if set), user's usage count < usage_limit_per_user (if set). Discount calculation: "
     "if discount_type=2 (percent): discount = (price + buyer_fee + extended_amount) * amount / 100. If "
     "discount_type=1 (fixed): discount = amount. Updates each cart row with coupon_id + discount. Stores "
     "coupon_total + coupon_id in session. Any cart modification (toggle extended, toggle addon, remove item) "
     "clears the coupon."),
    ("Checkout Flow (6 Steps)",
     "Step 1: User visits /checkout → CheckoutController@index. If guest: stores checkout_return_url in session, "
     "shows login/register prompt. If auth: loads cart items, calculates subtotal + total, loads active PayPal + "
     "Razorpay gateways (hardcoded filter — manual UPI shown separately). Step 2: User clicks 'Place Order' → "
     "processCheckout() validates auth + cart + own-product check + profile complete. Step 3: User selects "
     "gateway → POST /checkout/payment/process → processPayment() validates gateway, creates Order via "
     "createOrder(), creates Deposit, calls gateway ProcessController::process(). Step 4: User completes payment "
     "on gateway (Razorpay checkout modal OR PayPal redirect). Step 5: Gateway redirects back to /deposit/confirm "
     "OR sends webhook to /ipn/{gateway}. Step 6: PaymentController::userDataUpdate() credits balances, creates "
     "transactions, clears cart, redirects to /checkout/thank-you."),
    ("Order Creation (Atomic)",
     "CheckoutController::createOrder() (duplicated in PaymentController::createOrder() — code smell, should be "
     "extracted to service). Calculates: amount = sum(cart.price) - coupon_discount + sum(extended_amount) + "
     "sum(buyer_fee) + sum(addon_services_amount). Creates Order row with trx (unique 12-char). For each cart "
     "item: determines author's highest AuthorLevel (largest minimum_earning <= author.total_sold_amount), "
     "calculates seller_fee = level.fee% * price. Creates OrderItem with: purchase_code (unique format: "
     "{user_id}-{product_id}-{random}-{timestamp}), product_price, buyer_fee, seller_fee, license, extended_amount, "
     "addon flags, discount (per-item), seller_earning = (price - (seller_fee + discount)) + extended_amount + "
     "addon_amount. NOTE: seller_earning formula here is DIFFERENT from the one used in userDataUpdate() — this "
     "is a BUG in the original code (creates order item with one formula, then recalculates on payment success "
     "with a different formula). Migration must pick ONE formula and document it."),
    ("Wallet Payment Path",
     "If user has sufficient balance (user.balance >= order.amount), they can pay via wallet — gateway='wallet'. "
     "PaymentController::orderFromAccountBalance() bypasses gateway entirely: immediately sets "
     "order.payment_status=SUCCESS, deducts buyer.balance, creates buyer Transaction, credits each author, "
     "creates author Transactions, clears cart, triggers referral. This is a no-fee payment path (no gateway "
     "charge). Currently UI does not expose this option (CheckoutController filters to PayPal+Razorpay only), "
     "but the code path exists. Migration should expose wallet payment as a third option for users with balance."),
]

